NAME
    menu-ext-adv-fs - browse a filesystem tree with configurable action keys

SYNOPSIS
    menu-ext-adv-fs [-H <header>] [-F <footer>] [-B <bottom-footer>]
                    -K <key> [-K <key> ...] [-n] [-m] -- <path>

DESCRIPTION
    menu-ext-adv-fs presents an interactive directory browser built on
    menu-ext-adv.

    The starting path is canonicalized to an accessible directory. Enter moves
    into the selected directory. A configured action key returns:
        <key>@:=<absolute-selected-path>

    Escape cancels. Navigation keys and Enter are reserved. At least one custom
    -K key is required.

OPTIONS
    -H <header>         Header displayed above the current path.
    -F <footer>         Footer after the visible entries.
    -B <bottom-footer>  Footer anchored at the bottom.
    -K <key>            Configure an action key; may be repeated.
    -n                  Hide hidden directory entries.
    -m                  Mix directories and other entries in one lexical list.
    -h                  Write command usage.

EXIT STATUS
    0   A configured action key selected a path.
    1   The browser was cancelled.
    2   Invalid invocation, inaccessible path or dependency/setup failure.

SEE ALSO
    menu-ext-adv
